<div id="post-content">
    <article id="post-article" class="fade-in" style="opacity:1" >
        <h1 id="main-content">ChatChat — Open AI Chat Client</h1>

        <p>A no-build, single-page chat interface for OpenAI-compatible chat completion APIs. Point it at <a href="https://lmstudio.ai/" rel="noopener">LM Studio</a> running locally or a cloud provider, and you're chatting in seconds.</p>

        <p>No bundler. No package manager. No backend. Just HTML, CSS, and JS — open <code>index.html</code> and go.</p>

        <figure class="shot">
            <img src="img/hero-full.png" width="1280" height="800" loading="lazy"
                 alt="ChatChat hero screen — dark themed landing page with an orb, mode pills (Chat / Story), prompt starter chips, and the hero input box.">
            <figcaption>Open, type, send. That's it.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2>What it is</h2>
        <p>ChatChat is a chat UI I built because LM Studio's built-in interface is fine, but I wanted something with a bit more personality — a story mode for interactive fiction, better markdown rendering, import/export, configurable sampling parameters, and the ability to switch between a local model and a cloud provider without reloading.</p>

        <p>It's all client-side. Your chats, your config, your API keys — everything stays in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>. Nothing is sent anywhere except the messages you explicitly send to the API endpoint you configure.</p>

        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Chat mode</strong> — freeform conversation with any OpenAI-compatible API. System prompt, temperature, repetition penalty — all configurable.</li>
            <li><strong>Story mode</strong> — three styles of interactive fiction:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Adventure (CYOA)</strong> — second-person narration, every reply ends with 2-3 numbered choices.</li>
                    <li><strong>Roleplay</strong> — the AI plays your lead character and NPCs; you direct the story or speak in character.</li>
                    <li><strong>Game Master</strong> — the AI runs the scene like a tabletop GM, narrating outcomes for what you attempt.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li><strong>Streaming</strong> — responses appear token-by-token as they're generated, rendered at ~30fps to avoid layout thrash.</li>
            <li><strong>Markdown rendering</strong> — assistant responses render markdown with syntax-highlighted code blocks, powered by <code>marked</code> + <code>DOMPurify</code> + <code>highlight.js</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Regeneration</strong> — cycle through alternate responses for any message without losing the originals.</li>
            <li><strong>Compression</strong> — older turns can be summarized into a single message to keep context under control.</li>
            <li><strong>Provider switching</strong> — toggle between <strong>Local</strong> (LM Studio at <code>localhost:1234</code>) and <strong>NanoGPT</strong> (cloud) without reloading.</li>
            <li><strong>Import / Export</strong> — export all your chats as JSON, or import them back. Story configs export as JSON or plain text.</li>
        </ul>

