        <h2>Running it</h2>
        <p>
            Just open <code>index.html</code> in a browser, or serve the directory statically:
            <pre><code>python3 -m http.server</code></pre>
            For the default "Local" provider, <a href="https://lmstudio.ai/" rel="noopener">LM Studio</a> needs to be running at <code>http://localhost:1234</code> with a model loaded.
        </p>

        <h2>Tech stack</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Zero build tools — plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JS.</li>
            <li>CDN-loaded: <code>marked</code> (markdown parsing), <code>DOMPurify</code> (sanitization), <code>highlight.js</code> (syntax highlighting).</li>
            <li>Everything persists to <code>localStorage</code> — chats, settings, generation history, story configs.</li>
            <li>Provider abstraction: <code>local</code> (LM Studio) and <code>nanogpt</code> (cloud) registered in <code>state.js</code>.</li>
            <li>Two conversation modes with their own system prompt builders: <code>chat</code> (freeform) and <code>story</code> (CYOA / roleplay / GM).</li>
            <li>Streaming via raw SSE parsing — no SDK, no dependencies.</li>
        </ul>

